# Copy to .env for `docker compose up -d`, or enter these in Dokploy's Environment tab.
# Nothing in this file is a real secret.

# --- which model (REQUIRED) -------------------------------------------------------------------
# openai, anthropic or deepseek. Then give the key for that one.
TALARIA_PROVIDER=deepseek
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
#OPENAI_API_KEY=
#ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# A model name, if not the provider's default (deepseek-flash, gpt-4o-mini, claude-sonnet-5-5).
#TALARIA_MODEL=

# --- who may talk to it -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set the token of the service you use, and the user IDs allowed in (comma separated). With no IDs the
# bot only answers /whoami, which tells you yours. Only allow people you would trust with the agent's accounts.
TALARIA_DISCORD_TOKEN=
TALARIA_DISCORD_ALLOWED_USERS=
#TALARIA_TELEGRAM_TOKEN=
#TALARIA_TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_USERS=

# --- calendars (optional, read-only) ----------------------------------------------------------------
# In Google Calendar: Settings > the calendar > Integrate calendar > "Secret address in iCal format".
# Paste it as name=address; separate several with commas or spaces. The address is a SECRET: anyone who has it can
# read that calendar, so it belongs here and nowhere else. It is kept out of what the agent sees. Reset it in
# Google Calendar to cancel it.
#TALARIA_CALENDARS=personal=https://calendar.google.com/calendar/ical/.../private-.../basic.ics
# The zone times are shown in, such as Africa/Lagos. Without it, times are in UTC.
#TALARIA_TIMEZONE=Africa/Lagos

# --- email (optional, read-only) --------------------------------------------------------------------
# The agent can read your mail, and only read it: it cannot send, delete, move or mark anything. It signs in with an
# APP PASSWORD, not your normal password (Gmail: turn on 2-step verification, then myaccount.google.com/apppasswords;
# iCloud: appleid.apple.com > App-Specific Passwords). The app password is a SECRET: keep it here and nowhere else.
# Revoke it in your account to cancel it.
#TALARIA_EMAIL=you@gmail.com
#TALARIA_EMAIL_PASSWORD=
# The IMAP server, as host or host:port (always encrypted). Only needed when it cannot be found from the address:
# Gmail, iCloud, Fastmail, Yahoo, AOL, Zoho and Outlook.com are known.
#TALARIA_EMAIL_SERVER=imap.example.com
# Only if you sign in with something other than the address.
#TALARIA_EMAIL_USER=

# --- web app (optional): Talaria's own page, installable on your phone ----------------------------------
# Sign in with this password. It is all that stands between the internet and your agent: at least 12
# characters, and a few random words is a good way to make one. Keep it here and nowhere else.
#TALARIA_WEB_PASSWORD=
# The https address you reach it at (phones need https to install the app and to get notifications). In Dokploy,
# add the domain on the Domains tab: this service, port 8080, https.
#TALARIA_WEB_PUBLIC_URL=https://talaria.example.com
# Where it listens inside the container. The default is fine.
#TALARIA_WEB_LISTEN=:8080

# --- optional ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Opens the saved-logins vault with nobody there to type it. Create the vault first: see the README.
#TALARIA_VAULT_PASSPHRASE=
# More settings, as one line of JSON: connected services, limits, protected paths. Written to /data/config.json at every start.
# Keep secrets out of it: name the variable that holds each one ("api_key_env", "token_env").
#TALARIA_CONFIG_JSON={"limits":{"model_calls_per_hour":500}}
# Health and metrics. 127.0.0.1 is inside the container only; to let a monitor reach it, listen on 0.0.0.0:9100,
# set a token, and publish the port yourself.
#TALARIA_OPS_LISTEN=127.0.0.1:9100
#TALARIA_OPS_TOKEN=
# Shown by `tal version`.
#TALARIA_VERSION=
